  "summary": "While Oudinot fell back from Großbeeren, Girard marched out of Magdeburg with a column of depot battalions and German allies to join him. Hirschfeld, with a corps of Kurmark Landwehr only weeks old and a few regular battalions, caught him near Belzig and attacked round the village of Hagelberg in the rain. The Landwehr's muskets would not fire, and the fight at the village walls was settled with butts and bayonets; Girard's column broke, his cavalry fled, Chernyshev's Cossacks joined the pursuit, and little more than a third of it reached Magdeburg.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "label": "Prussian Order of Battle for Hagelberg, 27 August 1813 (Nafziger Collection 813HHC)",
