    {
      "id": "hagelberg-girard",
      "nationId": "france",
      "name": "Girard's Division",
      "formation": "Magdeburg Division (Lanusse), under Girard",
      "side": "French",
      "summary": "Girard's column out of Magdeburg, marching to join Oudinot's drive on Berlin: third battalions of French regiments, Westphalians, Saxon ducal troops and Croats. Caught round Hagelberg by Hirschfeld's Landwehr, it was broken in the village and among its walls and gardens, much of the fighting done with musket butts; Girard was wounded, and barely a third of his men got back to Magdeburg.",
      "notes": [
        "Built from A Clash of Eagles' French 1812 list, the nearest to 1813: there is no list for the army Napoleon raised after Russia, largely of conscripts and of battalions drawn from depots all over the Empire.",
        "After Nafziger's order of battle for Hagelberg.",
        "Lanusse commanded the Magdeburg Division under Girard, who led the whole column; Girard leads the force.",
        "The third and sixth battalions of regiments serving elsewhere, sent out from their depots, are grouped as the brigades' regiments, as the list takes them. The Croatian battalion is shown as Line.",
        "The 9th Westphalian and the Saxon ducal battalions are the list's Rheinbund infantry; two Rheinbund battalions in Baville's regiment, where the list takes one, show as a historical departure.",
        "The 13th Hussars had three squadrons, about 500 men.",
        "The division's two foot batteries, where the list allows one, show as a historical departure.",
        "Commanders are at Staff Rating 8, the default for historical forces."
      ],
